{{define "content"}}
<vox-hero eyebrow="Nodes and inventory" heading="Every node, and what it actually did" data-i18n-attr="heading,eyebrow">
  <p data-i18n>
    The console reads openvoxdb directly, so what you see is what your
    agents reported &mdash; nothing to sync, and nothing to change on the
    node side.
  </p>
</vox-hero>

<section class="site-section">
  <h2 class="vox-ts-xxl" data-i18n>Start with what needs attention</h2>
  <div class="vox-prose">
    <p data-i18n>
      Runs are grouped the way you would triage them: what failed, what
      changed on purpose, what corrected drift, and what was already as
      you asked. Reachability is tracked separately, because a node that
      has gone quiet and a node that reported a failure are different
      problems with different fixes.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

{{screenshot "dashboard"}}

<section class="site-section">
  <h2 class="vox-ts-xxl" data-i18n>Search the fleet by any fact</h2>
  <div class="vox-prose">
    <p data-i18n>
      Filter by name, or by anything your agents report &mdash; operating
      system, kernel, architecture, a custom fact of your own. Answers
      come from openvoxdb as it stands right now, not from a cache.
    </p>
    <p data-i18n>
      Certificate state sits alongside, and with CA access configured you
      can sign and revoke from the same page instead of finding a shell on
      the server.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

{{screenshot "nodes-list"}}

<section class="site-section">
  <h2 class="vox-ts-xxl" data-i18n>One node in full</h2>
  <div class="vox-prose">
    <p data-i18n>
      A node's own page gathers its facts, its recent runs, the classes
      classification gave it, what it has installed and which
      vulnerabilities touch it &mdash; everything you want when one
      machine, rather than the fleet, is the question.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

{{screenshot "node-detail"}}

<vox-callout variant="tip" heading="Reports keep their detail" data-i18n-attr="heading">
  <p data-i18n>
    Every resource event a run produced is here, with the old and new
    value for each change and the manifest and line that caused it. It is
    what the agent sent, not a summary of it.
  </p>
</vox-callout>
{{end}}
